---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from "../data/schema";

const siteBase = new URL("/", Astro.site).toString().replace(/\/$/, "");
const pageSchemas = webPageSchema(siteBase, {
  type: "AboutPage",
  name: "About SteadyFocusCo",
  description:
    "Planning and organization tools for overwhelmed minds. SteadyFocusCo creates printable planners and free digital tools for ADHD, students, and anyone who finds traditional planning systems don't work for them.",
  path: "/about",
  breadcrumb: breadcrumbSchema(siteBase, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "About", path: "/about" },
  ]),
});
---

<Base
  title="About SteadyFocusCo"
  description="Planning and organization tools for overwhelmed minds. SteadyFocusCo creates printable planners and free digital tools for ADHD, students, and anyone who finds traditional planning systems don't work for them."
>
  {pageSchemas.map((s) => (
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(s)}></script>
  ))}
  <section class="about-page">
    <div class="about-content">
      <h1>About SteadyFocusCo</h1>

      <p>
        SteadyFocusCo makes planning tools for people whose brains don't do linear.
        If you've ever stared at a pristine planner only to abandon it two weeks later,
        or if traditional to-do lists leave you feeling worse instead of organized —
        you're in the right place.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site offers free digital tools and printable resources designed for ADHD
        brains, busy students, and anyone who feels overwhelmed by conventional
        planning systems. Everything here is built around the idea that organization
        should work <em>with</em> how your brain actually functions, not against it.
      </p>

      <p>
        The free tools and printables on this site are companion resources to the
        SteadyFocusCo Etsy shop, where you'll find matching printable planners and
        organizational systems available for instant download. Whether you're here
        for the free tools or shopping for a complete planning system, the goal is
        the same: to help you build routines and systems that actually stick.
      </p>

      <p>
        No perfection required. No complicated systems to maintain. Just practical
        tools that meet you where you are.
      </p>

      <h2>What SteadyFocusCo is</h2>
      <p>
        SteadyFocusCo is a small collection of ADHD-friendly printable planners,
        free productivity tools, and practical guides. Everything here is built
        around one idea: the problem isn't that you're disorganized — it's that
        most planning systems assume a brain that starts tasks on command and
        remembers what it can't see. These tools take the opposite approach.
      </p>

      <h2>ADHD-friendly planners and printables</h2>
      <p>
        The printable planners in the <a href="/shop">shop</a> are designed for
        ADHD brains and anyone who finds traditional planners overwhelming. They
        focus on getting thoughts out of your head, making the next step obvious,
        and lowering the cost of starting — not on filling every box perfectly.
        You'll find brain dumps, homework trackers, study planners, executive
        function planners, and routine checklists, all available as instant
        digital PDF downloads.
      </p>

      <h2>Free productivity tools</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/tools">free tools</a> run entirely in your browser — no
        account, nothing stored, nothing sent anywhere. The
        <a href="/tools/brain-dump">Brain Dump</a> helps you empty your head and
        sort it into what to do now, what has a deadline, and what can wait. The
        <a href="/tools/weekly-reset">Weekly Reset</a> turns a scattered week into
        one calm plan. And the
        <a href="/tools/morning-routine">Morning Routine Builder</a> helps you
        build a short, realistic sequence you'll actually keep.
      </p>

      <h2>Executive function support</h2>
      <p>
        A lot of what makes planning hard comes down to executive function — the
        mental skills that help you start tasks, hold a plan in mind, and switch
        between steps. These tools and <a href="/guides">guides</a> are built to
        support that, whether you're a student facing a big assignment, an adult
        juggling work and home, or someone who just wants a calmer daily routine.
      </p>

      <h2>For students, work, and everyday life</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/students">student</a> resources focus on homework planning,
        assignment tracking, and breaking large projects into smaller steps so
        they feel startable. The <a href="/productivity">productivity</a> section
        covers weekly planning, prioritization, and routines that don't rely on
        willpower. And the <a href="/adhd">ADHD</a> section brings it all together
        for planning, organization, and reducing overwhelm at home and at work.
      </p>

      <h2>Print or annotate digitally</h2>
      <p>
        Every printable works two ways: print it at home and fill it in with a
        pen, or open the PDF on a tablet and annotate it digitally. Both are
        valid — the point is to get the plan out of your head and somewhere you
        can see it.
      </p>

      <h2>The philosophy</h2>
      <p>
        The goal is simple: help people take one small step at a time. You don't
        need a perfect system. You need a next step that's small enough to start.
        That's what SteadyFocusCo is here for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 3rem auto 4rem;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-content h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .about-content p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-content em {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .about-page {
      margin: 2rem auto 3rem;
    }

    .about-content p {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>